Here is provided code and software details, which includes pseudocode. Julia can be installed using the installation guide at https://julialang.org/install/.

Julia version: v1.11.5

Packages used: DifferentialEquations.jl, Ipopt.jl, JuMP.jl, LaTeXStrings.jl, LinearAlgebra.jl, Plots.jl

Results typically are generated on a "normal" desktop computer within a day.

bifurcation_diagram.jl
This code houses functions to calculate utility and replicator dynamics under proportional allocation of resources. It loops through different parameter values α to find stable and unstable equilibria. It then plots these in a figure.

diffusion equations.jl
This code houses functions to calculate utility and replicator dynamics under proportional allocation of resources. It numerically solves the replicator equations, calculates a variety of measures of social welfare, and plots these results in a heatmap and time series.

diffusion equations Nash.jl
This code is similar to diffusion equations.jl. Except, allocations are determined by optimizing the Nash social welfare, which is calculated using the JuMP.jp and Ipopt.jl packages.

diffusion equations heterogeneity.jl
This code houses a functions that calculate utility and the selection gradient (invasion fitness). It calculates the selection gradient for varying initial conditions and plots a heatmap of invasibility.
